# Identical workload to `particle_filter.qu`, EXCEPT it uses the `@`
# in-place-mutation prefix operator (`@pf.move(dt)` / `@pf.update(...)`)
# instead of plain reassignment (`pf = pf.move(dt)` / `pf = pf.update(...)`)
# -- see BACKLOG.md's "In-place mutation for `@expr.method()`" entry
# (2026-09-01). `pf = pf.move(dt)` CANNOT take the new in-place fast path
# (there is no `@`, so `qu-interp` never even attempts it -- see
# `Stmt::Assign`'s `in_place` field doc comment in qu-syntax); only this
# `@`-spelled version exercises `try_inplace_particle_tracker_move`/
# `_update`. Kept as a SEPARATE file from `particle_filter.qu` (not an
# edit to it) so the original plain-reassignment benchmark keeps measuring
# exactly what it always has.

seed(3)
N = 500
dt = 0.05
true_v = 1.5
t = (0 to N - 1) * dt
true_pos = true_v * t
measured = true_pos + 0.4 * randn(N)

n_particles = 50000

tic()
pf = particle_filter(n_particles, [0, 0], process_noise=0.08, obs_noise=0.4, spread=2.0, seed=3)
est_pos = zeros(1, N)
est_vel = zeros(1, N)
for k = 0 to N - 1
    @pf.move(dt)
    @pf.update([measured[k]])
    est = pf.estimate()
    est_pos[k] = est[0]
    est_vel[k] = est[1]
end for
elapsed_ms = toc() * 1000

raw_err = rms(measured - true_pos)
filt_err = rms(est_pos - true_pos)
print("[Qu @] Position RMS error: raw sensor={raw_err:.3f}, particle filter estimate={filt_err:.3f}")
print("[Qu @] True velocity={true_v:.2f}, final estimated velocity={est_vel[N-1]:.3f}")
print("[Qu @] elapsed={elapsed_ms:.1f} ms for {n_particles} particles x {N} steps (in-place @ syntax)")
